        "content": "**Normal**\n- **Daily snapshot-bot burst:** ~08:0x UTC, UA `node`, one Azure/GH-Actions IP, 1\u00d7 `/api/gamedays/?format=json&page_size=1000` then ~900\u00d7 `/api/gamedays/<id>/games/?format=json` in ~3 min. Stat panels \u00a77 read ~1 / ~900. Burst view spikes to ~300 req/min and falls back to ~0.\n- **Sideline polling:** UA `Sideline/1.0 (inoffizieller Spielplan-Client)`, low steady rate on `/api/gamedays/?search=season:2026&page_size=500` and `/games/`. No bursts.\n- **Browsers:** `Mozilla/*` spread across many ClientHosts, low per-IP rate, mixed endpoints, 2xx-dominated.\n\n**Deserves a look**\n- A **new UA** (or new ClientHost) bursting >100 req/min, esp. on `/api/gamedays*/games/`.\n- **429 spikes** (\u00a74): rate limiting is engaging \u2014 check whether it is the known bot (tune limits?) or an unknown client.\n- **5xx spikes**: nginx/gunicorn/Django upstream problem, not client behaviour \u2014 check LeagueSphere logs.\n- **p95 regression** on `/api/gamedays*/games/` (\u00a75) or payload jump (\u00a76): serialization / page_size / DB regression.\n\n**Alert proposals (OUT OF SCOPE for this task \u2014 candidates only)**\n1. `burst>100/min by unknown UA for 5m` (Loki metric query on \u00a73, exclude `node`+`Sideline`).\n2. `5xx rate on /api/* > threshold for 5m` (match the existing `traefik_service_requests_total{code=~\"5..\"}` Prometheus alerts).\n3. `p95(/api/gamedays*/games/) > SLO (e.g. 2\u00d7 baseline) for 15m` (recording rule on \u00a75 quantiles; needs longer retention first).",
